{id:"api-2014-magic-items-necklace-of-prayer-beads",name:"Necklace of Prayer Beads",content:[{id:"Title",content:"Necklace of Prayer Beads"},{id:"StatGrid",content:[{title:"Category",content:"Wondrous Items"},{title:"Rarity",content:"Rare"}]},{id:"TitledText",content:[{title:"",content:"Wondrous item, rare (requires attunement by a cleric, druid, or paladin)"},{title:"",content:"This necklace has 1d4 + 2 magic beads made from aquamarine, black pearl, or topaz. It also has many nonmagical beads made from stones such as amber, bloodstone, citrine, coral, jade, pearl, or quartz. If a magic bead is removed from the necklace, that bead loses its magic."},{title:"",content:"Six types of magic beads exist. The GM decides the type of each bead on the necklace or determines it randomly. A necklace can have more than one bead of the same type. To use one, you must be wearing the necklace. Each bead contains a spell that you can cast from it as a bonus action (using your spell save DC if a save is necessary). Once a magic bead's spell is cast, that bead can't be used again until the next dawn."},{title:"",content:"| d20 | Bead of... | Spell |"},{title:"",content:"|---|---|---|"},{title:"",content:"| 1-6 | Blessing | Bless |"},{title:"",content:"| 7-12 | Curing | Cure wounds (2nd level) or lesser restoration |"},{title:"",content:"| 13-16 | Favor | Greater restoration |"},{title:"",content:"| 17-18 | Smiting | Branding smite |"},{title:"",content:"| 19 | Summons | Planar ally |"},{title:"",content:"| 20 | Wind walking | Wind walk |"}]}]}